    "chunk_text": "LANKA AND THE UNITED STATES\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dad\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dda\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Speaker, first of all, may I wish the country and all Parliamentarians, including you, a very happy New Year!\n\nPublic statements by the United States President Donald Trump indicate an intention to conclude outstanding trade disputes and finalize bilateral trade agreements with partner countries, including Sri Lanka by March, 2026. Those negotiations assume heightened significance following the devastation caused by Cyclone \"Ditwah\", which has severely affected Sri Lanka\u2019s agriculture, industry, infrastructure and the export capacity, thereby impacting on our economic resilience and negotiating position.\n\nGiven the long-term fiscal, strategic and livelihood implications of any trade agreement, Parliament requires clarity, transparency and assurance that Sri Lanka\u2019s national interest is fully safeguarded.\n\nSir, I draw your attention to a news item published in the \"Daily Mirror\" online edition of 18th November, 2025, which reported what the Hon. Vijitha Herath had stated. It states, I quote:\n\n\"Sri Lanka still to come to agreement with U.S. on reciprocal tariffs: Minister\"\n\nSo, bearing that in mind, I have framed this Question, to which I seek clarification from the Prime Minister, who is not here at the moment.\n\n1. What is the current status of trade negotiations with the United States and have any timelines, draft frameworks or commitments been agreed upon in line with the target of March, 2026?\n\nSir, as you know, we basically do trade worth US Dollars 3.6 billion with the United States of America. Making frivolous statements would not help you get onto that type of negotiations, but we would, at least, know that we are heading somewhere.\n\n75 76\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd2 06"
